<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1797–1870</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold II was the last reigning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duke-of-tuscany">Grand Duke of Tuscany</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-habsburg-lorraine">House of Habsburg-Lorraine</a>, ruling from 1824 to 1859. His early reign was mild and reforming, with drainage of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maremma">Maremma</a> and a relatively free press, but after the revolutions of 1848–1849 he returned under Austrian protection. When war broke out between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> with Piedmont-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> in 1859 he left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, and Tuscany was annexed to the Kingdom of Sardinia in 1860.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-ii-grand-duke-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Benvenuti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_II_of_Tuscany.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
